        ],
        "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199233/observations/step-e8329-bcfcaedf02ea34d3e68c.html",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199233/observations/step-e8329-bcfcaedf02ea34d3e68c.png",
        "worked_solution": "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = 2x$ and $v(x)=\\tanh x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(2x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x\\cdot (\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x\\cdot {\\text{\\sech}}^{2}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x{\\text{\\sech}}^{2}x \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+x{\\text{\\sech}}^{2}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "can_dont_know": false,
        "can_skip": false,
        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-e8329",
          "name": "Example: Differentiating Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule",
          "problem": "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = 2x\\tanh{x}.$",
          "worked_solution": "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = 2x$ and $v(x)=\\tanh x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(2x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x\\cdot (\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x\\cdot {\\text{\\sech}}^{2}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2x{\\text{\\sech}}^{2}x \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+x{\\text{\\sech}}^{2}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
          "fields": [],
          "problem_field_keys": [],
          "answer_fields_complete": null,
