      {
        "key": "step-q95231",
        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-q95231",
          "name": "Question 2",
          "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.$",
          "worked_solution": "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)={sech}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
