        "solution_binding": "62496a8566b1b0f06a6e467cbc500dde121657a3d982192f00ec95b5f9fad920",
        "accepted": true,
        "feedback": {
          "dom_id": "step-q95671",
          "name": "Question 4",
          "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.$",
          "worked_solution": "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)={sech}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
