            }
          ],
          "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199233/observations/step-q95679-dc6a47db28d363f6ec8b.html",
          "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199233/observations/step-q95679-dc6a47db28d363f6ec8b.png",
          "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\sqrt{g},\\,g=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "can_dont_know": false,
          "can_skip": false,
          "question": {
            "dom_id": "step-q95679",
            "name": "Question 10",
            "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.$",
            "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\sqrt{g},\\,g=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
            "calculator_instructions": "",
