          "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199233/observations/step-q95273-013b8489f65d1b4773a5.html",
          "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14199233/observations/step-q95273-013b8489f65d1b4773a5.png",
          "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 2x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x}+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "can_dont_know": false,
          "can_skip": false,
          "question": {
            "dom_id": "step-q95273",
            "name": "Question 11",
            "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}.$",
            "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 2x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x}+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
            "calculator_instructions": "",
