        "solution": {
          "status": "ambiguous",
          "reasoning": "For x > 0, the product and chain rules give f'(x) = cosh(x²)/x + 2x ln(x)sinh(x²). Factoring out 1/x yields option b. No Math Academy answer or grade for the current question is captured.",
          "confidence": 1,
          "answers": [
            {
              "key": "selection",
              "correct_value": "\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2})",
              "correct_option": "b",
              "value_type": "math",
              "wrong_value": "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2}",
