      {
        "key": "step-q95235",
        "question": {
          "dom_id": "step-q95235",
          "name": "Question 18",
          "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.$",
          "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)^{′}}{(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "calculator_instructions": "",
